{
  "name": "std-tutorial-autodemo",
  "description": "Generic scripted input-replay atom: the demo half of a tutorial. Holds one or more named cue scripts (each an ordered list of { at, event, arg } rows where at is a millisecond offset and event is LEFT/RIGHT/JUMP/STOP); listens for TUTORIAL_DEMO_START { demoId } (from std-tutorial-overlay's demoId step) and plays the matching script on a 32ms clock, emitting the semantic DEMO_LEFT / DEMO_RIGHT / DEMO_JUMP / DEMO_STOP events the host board maps onto its own movement. TUTORIAL_DEMO_STOP, DEMO_CANCEL (real user input), or exhausting the cue list end the demo and emit DEMO_STOP so the character stops moving. Renders a small Demo badge while playing. Domain-agnostic: the demo never emits board events (OW_*, etc.) — the organism maps DEMO_* to its own steering, so a demo cannot self-cancel through the board's input path.",
  "level": "atom",
  "topic": "ui/game",
  "schema": {
